   "name": "Ports & Intermodal Logistics Dataset",
   "description": "The master dataset of the Ports & Intermodal program of The Flat Rate Movers: the six ports the company's crews serve with logistics project management, specialized labor, ocean container packing and unpacking, loading and unloading, cross-docking, transloading, 3PL support and freight rework — the Virginia Inland Port at Front Royal, the Port of Virginia at Norfolk (Norfolk International Terminals, Virginia International Gateway, Portsmouth Marine Terminal and Newport News Marine Terminal), Richmond Marine Terminal, the Port of Baltimore, the Port of Wilmington, Delaware, and PhilaPort at Philadelphia. Each port is a full entity: authority and operator of record, terminal facts with acreage, berths, depth and capacity where the port authority publishes them, cargo specialties, rail service with on-dock and interchange qualifiers, highway corridors, foreign-trade-zone facts where designated, labeled volume figures with their sources and periods, current status items, and the branch binding that assigns the port to Winchester, VA or Martinsburg, WV by verified road distance. Portsmouth Marine Terminal is recorded as what it is — a heavy-lift and offshore-wind hub, not a container terminal; Virginia International Gateway is recorded as leased, not port-authority-owned; the Port of Wilmington's operator of record is Enstructure. No volume figure is published for the Virginia Inland Port, Richmond Marine Terminal or the Port of Wilmington, because none is verified. The company's crews hold TWIC cards and its contractors hold valid TWIC cards. The offer set does not include drayage: the company does not run port drayage — freight moves on the customer's or carrier's trucks, and the company's crews do the hands-on work at port-adjacent warehouses, receivers' docks, yards, leased space, and on-terminal only by arrangement through the terminal's own processes. Every fact carries its source; the companion coverage-matrix node in this file maps all 48 port-by-service cells.",
